# Module Layout Rule: No `mod.rs`

- Do not create or keep `mod.rs` files.
- Define modules with file-named paths:
  - `foo.rs` for module `foo`
  - `foo/bar.rs` for module `foo::bar`
- In parent files, use plain declarations like `pub mod foo;` and let Rust resolve to `foo.rs`.
- For nested modules, prefer:
  - `foo.rs` + `foo/bar.rs`
  - not `foo/mod.rs` + `foo/bar.rs`
- When refactoring existing code, migrate any `mod.rs` module to `<module>.rs` and update references/paths accordingly.

## Example

```text
src/
  runtime.rs
  runtime/event_loop.rs
  runtime/input.rs
```

```rust
// src/runtime.rs
pub mod event_loop;
pub mod input;
```
